@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Ticket Routing when Organization is updated
	Testing Zendesk ticket organization information specifically from ticket updates.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I teardown the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "supportforlife"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	| ZENOSBE |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| no-reply@zenosba.com.broken         |
	| no-reply@zenosbe.com.broken         |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive  |
	| Zen OSB Engineering |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View account code and external id fields after organization update
	Zendesk tickets should have proper values for their accountCode and organizationExternalId fields

	Given I wait for "10" seconds
	And I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "supportforlife"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Premier            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	And I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Code         | ZENOSBE             |
	| Type         | Group               |
	| Industry     | Engineering         |
	| Tier         | Premier             |
	| Max Contacts | 10                  |
	| Address Line | 456 Fake Street     |
	| Country      | United States       |
	| State        | California          |
	| City         | Los Angeles         |
	| Zip          | 90013               |
	| Region       | US                  |
	| Language     | English             |
	And I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | osb.customer1                       |
	| Email Address | osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | OSB                                 |
	| Last Name     | Customer1                           |
	And I assign the web user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to the web organization "Customer"
	And I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBA"
	And I assign a user the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" as a customer with the role "Developer" to the project with the code "ZENOSBE"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBE"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I wait for "60" seconds
	And I update the user with the email address "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" to use the password "zendeskqauser"
	And I log into zendesk as "osb.customer1@lrcustomer.com.broken" with password "zendeskqauser"
	And I create a request with the following values
	| Product       | Liferay Portal                          | 6.2                                   |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration |                                       |
	| System Status | Production                              | Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Subject       | Request Subject                         |                                       |
	| Description   | Request Description                     |                                       |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                          |                                       |
	Then I should be able to view a request with the following details
	| Subject       | Request Subject                                    |
	| Status        | OPEN                                               |
	| Requester     | OSB Customer1                                      |
	| Priority      | Normal                                             |
	| Product       | Liferay Portal > 6.2                               |
	| Sub-Status    | —                                                  |
	| Component     | Activation Key & Project Administration            |
	| System Status | Production > Functioning with limited capabilities |
	| Attachments   | Document_1.txt                                     |
	And I should be able to view a request comment containing the text "Request Description" with the following details
	| Author      | OSB Customer1       |
	| Comment     | Request Description |
	| Attachments | Document_1.txt      |
	When I update the ticket with ticketId "${staticRequestIdList}" to have the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"
	Then the tickets with ticketIds "${staticRequestIdList}" should have the proper account code and externalId value of the organization "Zen OSB Engineering"